render-journal.js is 197 lines, 122 of them blank or comment. Those 122 were counted as "never
executed" by §36's reading of the same file.

── WHAT THIS INSTRUMENT CANNOT SEE, MEASURED (in §36's run; the blind spot is a property of
   `dsh web`, not of that run) ──
Running deepblend/tests/e2e/ui.e2e.mjs with NODE_V8_COVERAGE produces ZERO reports for the host
package: the `dsh web` process it starts does not write them. So every path reached only through
the UI reads as dark here. That is why listProjects, getRevisionDetail, getQaRecord and readArtifact
report count 0 — the browser suite exercises all four end to end (the panel lists projects, opens a
revision, shows QA, and fetches artifact bytes), and the routes that call them are served by that
invisible process.

    listProjects        0        getScene      6
    getRevisionDetail   0        listJobs      8
    readArtifact        0        getQaRecord   0

Read a dark line as "no test I can see executes this", not as "nothing executes this".

── WHAT THE READING SAYS ──
Most of the dark lines are error handling: catch blocks, "the encoder is missing" fallbacks, the
unreadable-record branch of the reconciler. That is the expected shape — an error path runs only
when something goes wrong, and a suite that made every error path run would be a suite that breaks
things on purpose (which is what the round-22 disk probe did, by hand, for one of them).

The whole bodies that are dark for a different reason — `listProjects`, `getRevisionDetail`,
`readArtifact`, `getQaRecord` — are reachable only from a process this instrument cannot see. That
is a fact about the measurement, and it is written down here rather than left to be inferred from a
number.

── WHAT THE TOOL NOW REFUSES TO DO (both learned the hard way, §37) ──
It exits non-zero and keeps its evidence when the SUITE exited non-zero, echoing the failing lines:
a reading of a red tree is not a reading, and the version that threw the suite's output away left
`suite exit code: 1` as the only trace of a 15-minute failure with no way to see which suite it was.

It also exits non-zero and names the files when a PRODUCT SOURCE FILE CHANGED while the suite ran.
Coverage is line numbers from the processes read against source text from disk, and those are two
different moments: a run that overlapped an edit reported a function called seven times by a test as
"never executed", and listed comment lines as the dark ones.
